  ('59ecc1ab-7c98-5225-bfa8-f2cdb9033d17', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'geometry-proofs'), null, 'medium',
   $q$Lines $a$ and $b$ are cut by a transversal. A pair of same-side interior angles measure $72^\circ$ and $106^\circ$. Which statement is true?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The lines are parallel, because same-side interior angles do not need to be equal","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignored-the-supplementary-requirement"},{"text":"The lines are not parallel, because $72 + 106 \\neq 180$","is_correct":true},{"text":"The lines are parallel, because $72 + 106$ is close to $180$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"accepted-an-approximate-sum"},{"text":"The lines are not parallel, because same-side interior angles of parallel lines are congruent","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"thought-same-side-interior-are-congruent"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The lines are not parallel, because $72 + 106 \neq 180$$q$, $q$Lines are parallel exactly when same-side interior angles are supplementary. Here $72 + 106 = 178$, not $180$, so the lines are not parallel. Same-side interior angles of parallel lines add to $180^\circ$; they are not congruent unless both are right angles.$q$, 'draft', null)
