  ('effbd66b-6be3-57f8-bb05-ecc6daf98fc7', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'geometry-proofs'), null, 'medium',
   $q$Two parallel lines are cut by a transversal. A pair of alternate exterior angles measure $(5x - 12)^\circ$ and $(3x + 20)^\circ$. What is the measure of each angle?$q$, $q$[{"text":"$95.5^\\circ$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"treated-alternate-exterior-as-supplementary"},{"text":"$68^\\circ$","is_correct":true},{"text":"$112^\\circ$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"gave-the-supplement"},{"text":"$16^\\circ$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"gave-x-instead-of-the-angle"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$$68^\circ$$q$, $q$Alternate exterior angles formed by parallel lines are congruent: $5x - 12 = 3x + 20$, so $2x = 32$ and $x = 16$. Each angle is $5(16) - 12 = 68^\circ$. Setting the sum to $180$ gives $x = 21.5$ and $95.5^\circ$, but these angles are equal, not supplementary.$q$, 'draft', null)
